important developing news on the  potential sale of chelsea by roman  abramovich now as i understand it mr  abramovic in the last couple of days has  demanded that the three remaining  bidders for chelsea football club stump  up an extra 500 million pounds if they  want to get their hands on the club now  this process has been going on uh since  uh mr mr abramovic was sanctioned by the  british government  at the beginning of march and at that  point uh just prior to his sanctioning  uh the current chelsea owner had said  that he intended to write off a one and  a half billion pounds loan uh to the  club that had built up over his 19 years  of ownership i am now told that that  writing off that loan for giving that  loan  is now legally not possible because of  mr abramovic's sanctioning and also  because he doesn't personally have  access to the funding required uh to  repay that loan himself now what all  this means is that the three remaining  bidders they are consortia uh headed by  the likes of uh uh sir martin broughton  the former liverpool and british airways  chairman uh and another uh consortium  which is headed by the boston celtics  part owner  steve palucca they have been told that  they will need to find this extra money  in the coming days if they are to win  the auction of chelsea my understanding  is that all three of the bidders remain  in the process and mr abramovic i am  told uh has authorized his associates to  oversee this final stage of the auction  process uh and has told the bidders that  he wants this extra 500 million pounds  to be donated to charity now there are  still lots of financial uncertainties  surrounding the sale process it's not  like 500 million pounds is money you can  easily find uh as loose change down the  back of a sofa jane so whether the three  bidders will be able to come up with  these extra funds in the coming days is  unclear we were expecting a preferred  bidder to emerge in the next few days it  remains to be seen whether that can uh  now happen but as i say the demand from  roman abramovich is that the three  remaining bidders for chelsea football  club do find an extra 500 million pounds  to add to the price that they are  prepared  to buy at last season's champions league  winners
 

